     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Next tests by pattern:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " chemistries, ferritin, haptoglobin, direct antiglobulin test, folate, B12, UA, fecal occult blood, and sometimes bone marrow aspiration and bx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sus lead poisoning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " CBC, lytes, BUN, creatinine, glucose and whole blood lead level; abd XR for lead particles; long-bone XRs in children."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Microcytic or normocytic anemia"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " suggests lead toxicity, esp w a ↑retic count or basophilic stippling."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cap lead tests"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " are fine for screening; confirm any (+) w a blood lead level (PbB)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
